 action, then call POST /api/v1/webhook/inboxes/{id}/wait with a timeoutMs (default 30 s, maximum 120 s). It returns the request as soon as it is stored, or a 408 if none arrives. Your test asserts on what came back. What happens if the webhook never arrives? + The wait call returns HTTP 408 with WAIT_TIMEOUT after your timeout. It never returns an empty 200, so a missing webhook fails your test with a clear reason. Is my inbox URL private? + Anyone with the URL can send to it, because providers can't sign in. Listing and reading events needs your DevHelm login or API key. Can I control what the sender receives? + Yes. Set the status (200 to 599), content type, body and a reply delay of up to 30 seconds for each inbox, for example a 500 to see how a provider retries. Extra headers can be set through the API. Can I test Stripe webhooks without ngrok? + Yes for receiving them: paste the inbox URL into the Stripe dashboard and send a test event. No tunnel needed because the inbox is a public URL. If you need Stripe to reach your local handler, you still need a tunnel for that. Is it free? What does it cost? + There is a free plan: 3 inboxes, 300 stored events a month and 3 days of history. Paid plans are $19, $79 and $149 per month, and annual billing gets two months free. Book a demo Delete the sleep.  Wait for the webhook. The beta is open by invitation. Book a 30-minute demo and we'll set up your workspace. TERMINAL $ curl -sSf -X POST https://api.devhelm.io/api/v1/webhook/inboxes/$INBOX_ID/wait \
